  "verdict": "NO HONEST IMPROVEMENT over the audited prior best (0.681). Best new method QN_crossStudy_quantile_L1=0.693, paired delta CI [-0.033935031244401476, 0.07459551184965542] includes 0 (or point estimate below prior best). Stronger domain adaptation (cross-study quantile normalization, CORAL second-order alignment, per-study standardization on ranks) does NOT beat simple per-sample rank normalization + sparse L1 on this 12-study set. The residual gap to within-study 0.858 reflects genuine study-to-study biological/chemistry heterogeneity (different toxicants, doses, tissues, developmental stages), which alignment of marginal/second-order feature statistics cannot remove without the held-out study's labels."
